 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (HVAC)",
 "applies_to": "Johnson Controls Variable Speed Drive Series III (VS3) HVAC drives using the on-board RS-485 port (BACnet MS/TP) or the RJ45 Ethernet port (BACnet IP).",
 "summary": "The VSD Series III has BACnet MS/TP on its RS-485 terminals (P12.3.1.1 RS485 Comm Set = 1) and BACnet IP on its RJ45 port (P12.4.1.9 Enable BACnet IP = 1). Both sections of the manual print the same object list: BVs for drive status, run/stop, direction, reset, control and speed source select, bypass and fire mode, digital I/O; AVs for the speed reference, limits, ramps, AnyParam access and process data in; AIs for monitors and process data out; and MVs for control mode and active fault.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "From the Variable Speed Drive Series III Communication Manual LIT-12013000 (September 2018): BACnet MS/TP Tables 58-61 (PDF pp55-57) and the BACnet IP section (PDF pp87-89), which print the same 78 objects.",
  "Enabling BACnet IP turns off BACnet MS/TP.",
  "AV 6/AV 7 AnyParam: write a parameter ID to AV 6 and read or write its value in AV 7.",
  "AV 8-15 and AI 18-25 are raw fieldbus process data; their content follows the P12.1/P12.2 process data selections.",
  "BV 21-23 (Digital Output 2-4) are described as relay outputs 1-3.",
  "C = commandable (priority array and relinquish default), per the manual."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Variable Speed Drive Series III Communication Manual (BACnet MS/TP and BACnet/IP on-board communication)",
  "doc_number": "LIT-12013000",
  "revision_date": "2018-09",
  "url": "https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/bas/api/khub/documents/XEo1PHGCK4nHiMO7HUpp~w/content"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "For MS/TP set P12.3.1.1 = 1 (BACnet MS/TP), then the baud rate, MAC address, instance number and Max Master in P12.3.3. For BACnet IP set the IP mode and static address in P12.4.1 and P12.4.1.9 = 1, then the UDP port and instance in P12.4.3. Write BV 7 and BV 8 to fieldbus control, then BV 9 run/stop and AV 0 speed reference; read BV 1, AI 1, AI 5 and BV 3.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 9",
    "name": "Run/Stop CMD",
    "why": "Start/stop command (Run = start)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 7",
    "name": "Motor Ctrl source",
    "why": "Must be FBMotorCtrl for network run/stop"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 0",
    "name": "Speed Reference",
    "why": "Speed reference, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 8",
    "name": "Speed Reference Source",
    "why": "Must be FBSpeedRef for the network reference"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 11",
    "name": "Reset Fault",
    "why": "Reset a tripped drive"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 1",
    "name": "Run/Stop State",
    "why": "Running status"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 1",
    "name": "Output Frequency",
    "why": "Output frequency, Hz"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 5",
    "name": "Motor Current",
    "why": "Motor amps"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 3",
    "name": "Fault State",
    "why": "Any active drive fault"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 1",
    "name": "Active fault code",
    "why": "Active fault code"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BV 7 Motor Ctrl source selects local or fieldbus (FBMotorCtrl) control of run/stop, and BV 8 Speed Reference Source selects local or fieldbus (FBSpeedRef) speed reference. MV 0 shows whether the drive is in Local (Hand), Remote or OFF.",
  "heartbeat": "MS/TP: Comm Timeout BACnet (P12.3.3, default 10000 ms) raises a communication error if the drive is sole master for that long. BACnet IP: BACnet IP Comm Timeout (P12.4.3, 0 = no supervision) raises a fieldbus fault after that many seconds without messages; the parameter table prints default 0, while the text says the default is 10 s. A pulled Ethernet cable faults at once. The Modbus RTU/BACnet Fault Response and BACnet IP Fault Behavior parameters choose whether the fault is raised only in fieldbus control (0, default) or in all control places (1).",
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "MS/TP: P12.3.1.1 RS485 Comm Set = 1; BACnet baud rate default 38400 (9600-115200); MAC address 0-127, default 1; Max Master default 127.",
   "MS/TP: the instance number (0-4194302) is set in P12.3.3; its default varies by drive.",
   "BACnet IP: P12.4.1.1 IP Address Mode (default 1 = DHCP with AutoIP, 0 = static); static defaults 192.168.1.254 / 255.255.255.0 / gateway 192.168.1.1. A change of IP mode needs a power cycle.",
   "BACnet IP: P12.4.1.9 Enable BACnet IP = 1 (default 0) shows the P12.4.3 settings: UDP port (47808-47823), foreign device, BBMD IP/port, registration interval (default 10 s) and instance number.",
   "Segmentation is not supported; the drive is a B-ASC."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "BACnet IP and BACnet MS/TP cannot run at the same time.",
   "BV 28 Force Bypass and BV 29 Fire Mode are commandable over BACnet.",
   "The manual's MS/TP parameter table is laid out unclearly; confirm parameter codes on the keypad (Main Menu > Parameter > Communication > RS485 Bus)."
  ]
 },
